<title>SINGAPORE: Eltech returns to profit in 1996.</title>
<headline>Eltech returns to profit in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Full year ended Dec 31 1996.</p>
<p>(in millions  of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit			 0.05   vs  (10.94)</p>
<p>    Earnings per share (cents)   0.03   vs   (7.88)</p>
<p>    Turnover			 112.21   vs  103.20</p>
<p>    Other income		     0.23   vs    0.28</p>
<p>    Interest expense		 1.39   vs    2.30</p>
<p>    Operating pretax		 0.46   vs   (9.43)</p>
<p>    Associates			(0.20)  vs   (1.31)</p>
<p>    Tax				  0.22   vs    0.21</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		  2.99   vs   (3.16)</p>
<p>Note - Eltech Electronics Ltd said its extraordinary gain came from profit derived from the sale of a property in Singapore, after deducting restructuring costs and provision for diminution in value of some long-term equity invetsments.</p>
<p>The group provides manufacturing services to electronics equipment manufacturers. 1995 earnings per share have been adjusted for a rights issue in 1996.</p>
<p>--Singapore newsroom (65-8703080)</p>
</text>
